; What a format hole refuses, every case under AX3025 so the code a
; reader already looks for still finds it. `(println x)` below is the
; hole: it lowers to the same reserved head `(format x)` does, and the
; refusal is the checker's, made from the argument's static type.
;
;   1  a type VARIABLE - a generic function's own `a`. A rendering is
;      chosen from a STATIC type and a variable is not one
;   2  a constructor applied to a type variable - `(Box a)` inside a
;      generic function - the same refusal one level in, and the
;      message says which type mentions the variable
;   3  a `data` or `struct` the checker cannot take apart: `Holder`
;      holds a `Foreign`, and the refusal names the field type and
;      lands at the CALL, before anything is generated
;
; The three read `show` until 0.7.4 and read `format` now, because the
; head they refuse is no longer a name a program can write. The SLUG
; moved with them - `trait-impl` was the last trait word on the
; user-facing surface - while the NUMBER did not: `check-doc-drift.sh`
; compares constructed codes against explained ones both directions,
; so retiring one is a two-sided move and this is not it.
(import IO)

(:: generic (-> a Int))

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (generic x)
  {
    (println x)
    0
  }
)

(struct Holder
  (f : Foreign))

(data Box a
  (MkBox a))

(:: boxed (-> (Box a) Int))

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (boxed b)
  {
    (println b)
    0
  }
)

(:: main Int)

;@axiom:effect(io)
(fn (main)
  (let ((h 
    (Holder
      (cast Foreign 0)
    )
  ))
    {
      (println h)
      0
    }
  )
)
